==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|γαστήρ||belly}} + {{der|en|grc|ἔντερον||intestine}} + {{der|en|grc|-λογία}}; synchronically, {{affix|en|gastro-|enterology}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} The study of the [[digestive]] system, from the [[mouth]] to the [[anus]]; may also include the study of [[accessory]] [[organ]]s: [[pancreas]], [[liver]], [[gallbladder]] and [[bile duct]]s.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|gastroenterologist}}

